KG42.register("clusters-755886e40fcef677c7487874",{"id":"24-brooklyn_microgrid::v142-d-K003","paper":"24-brooklyn_microgrid","label":"Two-sided offers, matching allocation, and uniform-price payment","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K003","label":"Two-sided offers, matching allocation, and uniform-price payment","market_meaning":"In the closed-order-book double-auction branch described by the BMG, participants submit prices and electricity quantities through the EMTS, the market mechanism matches and allocates accordingly, the last allocated offer forms the uniform price for that period, and after matching is completed funds are transferred according to the established payment arrangement. The existing chains establish candidate interfaces for input, allocation, pricing, and payment, but are not yet sufficient to determine a complete executable algorithm.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["bidding","matching","clearing","pricing","settlement"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"The main assembly connects only the BMG double auction and the illustrated payment branch. The general C4 design suggestion remains a suggestion; the feed-in tariff restriction of R003 retains the purely economic motive condition. The three-month fixed-price trial in R010 did not actively use the market mechanism, and the future pay-as-you bid also has separate conditions; both are retained in the original chain and do not apply to the uniform-price interface of this cluster.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"Order attributes enter matching allocation, and the allocation result determines the price and payment counterparties, constituting a market transaction arrangement with explicit information dependencies. The cross-stage connections come from the content of allocation, pricing, and payment, not from node connectivity; participant automatic strategies and physical islanded energy supply are retained separately.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provide demand order content and the reporting-stage consumer maximum-price offer strategy."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R003","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provide supply order content and minimum-price offers, and separately retain the conditional feed-in tariff discussion."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Take on orders, allocation priority relationships, and time-period structure, while retaining the not-yet-closed general constraints and additional energy branch."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R007","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Specify buy and sell orders as inputs for counterparty matching, supplementing the matching activity between allocation and payment."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R010","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provide the formation rule for the uniform clearing price; the fixed-price trial and the future individual-price branch within the original chain are retained independently according to their conditions."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R012","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Take on allocated participants, transaction price, and matching completion conditions, providing the illustrated payment relationships."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-order-price","v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-y-order-quantity"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g02-e35"],"rationale":"The price and electricity quantity submitted by the demand chain are the order content processed by the allocation chain, and the priority of higher buy prices is supplemented by the allocation passage; the two chains respectively describe submission behavior and allocation use, and cannot be deleted as duplicate constraints."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-order-price","v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-y-order-quantity"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e09","v141-b-g02-e35"],"rationale":"The minimum offer and supplied electricity quantity in the supply chain enter market allocation; this interface does not add sell-order ordering, transaction thresholds, or feed-in tariff values."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L03","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003","v141-c-R004::E::v141-c-R004-E004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e09"],"rationale":"C4 explicitly treats buy and sell order matching as the implementation mode of energy allocation, supporting the functional assembly of matching inputs and allocation activity; no optimization objective is added from this, nor is optimality guaranteed."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L04","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C008","v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-order-price"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C001","v141-c-R010::x::x_last_bid_t","v141-c-R010::x::x_clear_t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g02-e16"],"rationale":"The last allocated offer in the allocation result is used for pricing in that auction period; here it is an interface from the selection result to the price, not an identity equivalence between all order offers and the clearing price."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L05","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R012","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R007::V::matching.counterparties","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C003","v141-c-R012::E::v141-c-R012-E003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e09","v141-b-g02-e35"],"rationale":"The BMG workflow explicitly states that payment occurs after matching is completed, and R007 supplements the order input for matching; this connection only aligns existing activities and conditions and does not add a temporal edge in C."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L06","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R012","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::V::clearing.local","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C001","v141-c-R012::E::v141-c-R012-E001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e09","v141-b-g02-e17","v141-b-g03-e022"],"rationale":"Payment occurs among allocated participants, so the allocation result provides an interface for payment counterparties; the physical-layer feed explanation does not constitute a transaction-by-transaction electricity delivery path."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L07","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R012","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-y-order-quantity","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R012::theta::theta_y_consumer","v141-c-R012::theta::theta_y_producer","v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g03-e021"],"rationale":"The illustrated payment uses the order electricity quantities of consumers and prosumers respectively. The generalized order quantity in R004 and the two role parameters in R012 establish only input correspondences; the electricity quantities of buyers and sellers are not merged as a whole, nor is a remaining-quantity rule for continuous matching derived from the illustration."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-L08","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R012","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R010::x::x_clear_t","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R012::theta::theta_x_clearing","v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C002","v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g03-e021"],"rationale":"In the same BMG uniform-price period and the corresponding illustrated transaction, the pricing output becomes the payment price input; this correspondence does not extend to the fixed-price trial or future pay-as-you bid transactions."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-O01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R004::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R007::V::bidding.demand"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R002::V::bidding.demand","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e09","v141-b-g02-e35"],"rationale":"The three places cite the same demand submission function and are used respectively in submission, allocation, and matching contexts. The representative is used only for node display; the conditions, attributes, and edges of each chain are fully retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-O02","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R004::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R007::V::bidding.supply"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R003::V::bidding.supply","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e09","v141-b-g02-e35"],"rationale":"The three places cite the same supply submission function; selecting a display representative does not merge the supply limit-price conditions with the matching and allocation rules."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-O03","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::V::clearing.local","v141-c-R010::V::clearing.local","v141-c-R012::V::clearing.local"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e17"],"rationale":"The allocation function in the same auction branch appears respectively in the descriptions of allocation, price formation, and payment counterparties; the local role of each place is retained, and not all price branches of R010 are attributed to clearing."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-O04","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::V::matching.counterparties","v141-c-R007::V::matching.counterparties","v141-c-R012::V::matching.counterparties"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e09","v141-b-g02-e35"],"rationale":"The three places use the same matching function node, but the general design objective, order input, and BMG payment condition are not the same constraint; separate citations are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-O05","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R010::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R012::V::pricing.local"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e31","v141-b-g03-e016"],"rationale":"These citations use the same pricing function node, but involve additional energy supply conditions, the uniform price, the fixed-price trial, and future individual prices. Node consistency does not mean that all price objects or conditions are consistent, and the related edges and expressions cannot be merged."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K003-O06","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R010::x::x_clear_t","v141-c-R012::theta::theta_x_clearing"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g03-e021"],"rationale":"Only in the corresponding BMG uniform-price auction period do both point to the clearing price for that period. R010 retains the price formation variable role, R012 retains the payment input parameter role, and the original time index and unit fields are not rewritten."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G01","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The order index set, equal-price handling, sell-order acceptance conditions, partial and no-transaction handling, matching feasible region, and allocated electricity quantity are all not closed. The general minimum and maximum allocation requirements have no values or variables; the efficiency objective, cross-time-domain arrangement, and near-real-time suggestion also have no executable expression. The existing period length is insufficient to provide a complete timetable.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004","v141-c-R007","v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C005","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C006","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C007","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C008","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C001","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002","v141-c-R010::x::x_last_bid_t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e09","v141-b-g02-e10","v141-b-g02-e11"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Following the existing C2 revision request, re-extract the supportable sets, allocation steps, constraints, and time conditions; clarify the pricing when there is no transaction and the selection rule for the last allocated offer. Content not provided by the source remains blank."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G02","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The additional energy branch retains the original do not undercut condition, but lacks an explicit comparison object, boundary cases, energy supply eligibility, allocated quantity, and selection rules between similar bidding and predetermined prices; it cannot be rewritten as an automatic make-up mechanism for unallocated consumers.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004","v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C004","v141-c-R004::E::v141-c-R004-E003","v141-c-R010::x::x_clear_t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e11"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream should verify the exact meaning of this condition and obtain the eligibility, price, and quantity rules for additional energy; do not reverse the comparison relationship or add a make-up equation on your own."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G03","category":"scope_conflict","description":"R010 simultaneously contains the uniform-price design, the fixed-price trial that did not actively use the market mechanism, and the pay-as-you bid branch to be tested. The original chain cannot be split or altered, so these branches cannot serve as price constraints that take effect simultaneously at the same time point.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004","v141-c-R010","v141-c-R012"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C001","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C006","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C007","v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e15","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e31","v141-b-g03-e016","v141-b-g03-e024"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the branch conditions and implementation stages. This time only the uniform-price branch is connected to the illustrated payment; if other complete mechanisms need to be displayed independently, upstream should separately form chains with their respective applicable conditions."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G04","category":"math_incomplete","description":"What R012 retains is the illustrated price and paired electricity quantity arrows, not a separately given payment amount equation. The illustrated minimum order quantity does not explain the remaining-quantity update in multiple pairings, repeated-use restrictions, or settlement account changes, and cannot serve as a complete quantity allocation algorithm.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004","v141-c-R007","v141-c-R012"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-y-order-quantity","v141-c-R012::theta::theta_y_consumer","v141-c-R012::theta::theta_y_producer","v141-c-R012::phi::v141-c-R012-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e17","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e35"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Obtain the basis for actual traded volume, remaining-order updates, and monetary accounting, and check the applicable scope of the illustration; do not arbitrarily transcribe the arrows into a new payment equation or cyclic matching rule."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G05","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"The order price and electricity quantity in R004, and v141-b-g02-e21 cited by some expressions, actually discuss identity verification and cannot support order units or set definitions. The supplied original sentences also do not directly write out R004's generalized set and ordering notation, or R010's descriptive price equation notation; their existing source labels require upstream checking, and the frozen content remains unchanged this time.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004","v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-order-price","v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-y-order-quantity","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C001","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g03-e021","v141-b-g03-e016"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"B should verify the evidence locations, and C should check the formalized source labels and the scope of symbol generalization in a later version. The new interfaces in D use only content-relevant order, price, and illustration citations, and do not use the identity verification citation to support order mathematics."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G06","category":"ontology_extension","description":"The framework definitions of the existing demand and supply nodes describe only quantity submission and cannot fully express participant maximum or minimum price-limit attributes; the price-limit proposal has not yet been approved and cannot be replaced by the clearing price node.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002","v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-order-price"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g03-e011","v141-b-g03-e017","v141-b-g03-e020"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g03-p04"],"required_work":"Manually deliberate whether the price limit should be an attribute or an independent object, and then have C adjust the subsequent representation; this time the existing objects and their local roles are retained."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G07","category":"unverified_source","description":"All assembled interfaces are supported only by experimentally permitted unreviewed evidence. The illustration transcription, price meanings, and allocation interpretations have not passed independent source or scientific review.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R007","v141-c-R010","v141-c-R012"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e04","v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e09","v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g02-e16","v141-b-g02-e17","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e35","v141-b-g03-e021"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check each chain and all interfaces, focusing on the illustrated payment, the original-text allocation conditions, and the three pricing situations; retain the unverified status and do not treat candidate interfaces as verified algorithms."}]},"rule_refs":["24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R002","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R003","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R004","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R007","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R010","24-brooklyn_microgrid::v141-c-R012"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-6057789601b08e93","COMP-9ca8822ee86e3e13","COMP-d90b7b5c0051250f","COMP-ffbf050cce03a2e6","KG40-12aedc3eec573697","KG40-20f45ec4bdcbac06"]});
